{
"Ah! As for loving the chrysanthemum — since Tao one seldom hears of it.": "67c565d656ff",
"Among the flowering plants of water and land, there are a great many worth loving.": "0ca0564c4443",
"As for loving the lotus — who else is there with me?": "cbf8a359e617",
"As for loving the peony — of course that is the crowd's.": "1f2124e93dd7",
"I alone love the lotus: how it rises out of the mud and is not stained,": "014ad16ddd3b",
"Since the Li house of T'ang, the world has been much in love with the peony.": "dd9210ff6ab8",
"Tao Yuanming of the Chin loved the chrysanthemum alone.": "1e81556ccae6",
"To my mind the chrysanthemum is the recluse among flowers;": "92e11ca93744",
"and the lotus is the noble person among them.": "db3bb6af6b0e",
"hollow within and straight without, putting out no runners and no branches,": "42e907322130",
"how it is washed by clear ripples and yet is not made showy,": "3ff85f369ba4",
"its fragrance carrying far and growing purer with distance, standing tall and clean,": "d36300f7cfef",
"the peony is the one of wealth and rank;": "4f7b56d23358",
"to be looked at from a distance but not to be handled for amusement.": "8ae262c8f824"
